# Chapter Three — the Old Quarter.
# Question: what was wrong with the Prism before it vanished?
# Beat: the ledger. Iris ordered repair braces and paid for them herself.

@node ch3_lane_open
  The Old Quarter is all one lane, and the lane has been leaning companionably
  against itself since before anyone can remember.
  In colour it would be red brick and rust and geranium. In gray it is a
  pencil drawing of somewhere warm.

@node edwina_intro
  [if flag ch3.met_edwina == 0]
  EDWINA(shifty): No.
  YOU:
    * (dry) I have not asked anything yet.  -> edwina_notyet
    * (kind) That is all right. I can come back.  -> edwina_soft
    * (curious) No to which question?  -> edwina_notyet
  [else]
  goto edwina_after
  [end]

@node edwina_soft
  EDWINA(sad): ...No. Stay. I am sorry. I have said no eleven times today and
  it has got away from me.
  trust edwina 1
  goto edwina_niece

@node edwina_notyet
  EDWINA(worried): You were going to ask about my niece and I was going to say
  no, and now we have both saved a great deal of time.
  goto edwina_niece

@node edwina_niece
  set ch3.met_edwina = 1
  EDWINA: Iris is my sister's girl. She has been the Tinter since she was
  twenty-two and she has never once asked anybody for anything.
  YOU:
    * (curious) Did she ask you for something?  -> edwina_ask
    * (kind) That sounds lonely, rather than admirable.  -> edwina_lonely
    * (dry) A family trait, I imagine.  -> edwina_lonely

@node edwina_lonely
  EDWINA(moved): ...It is both. It has always been both. In this family we
  are very good at both.
  trust edwina 1
  goto edwina_ask

@node edwina_ask
  EDWINA(worried): She asked me for work. Paying work, and she would not have
  it any other way, and I let her, because I am a fool who thought it was
  pride.
  EDWINA: The clock in the window has been stopped a fortnight and I cannot
  face it. Put the train right and I will open the ledger for you.
  start_puzzle gear_train
  EDWINA(happy): Hm. You have a feel for it. Iris had a feel for it.
  EDWINA(sad): Third page. There. Her hand, my ledger.
  grant clue.cogg_ledger
  EDWINA: Four crystal repair braces. Brass, lined, made to a drawing she
  brought me. Ordered in the spring. Paid for out of her own pocket, in
  instalments, like a woman buying a coat.
  grant clue.repair_braces
  YOU:
    * (curious) Braces for what? You must have asked.  -> edwina_asked
    * (kind) You have been carrying this by yourself.  -> edwina_carry
    * (dry) A coat would have been cheaper.  -> edwina_asked

@node edwina_carry
  EDWINA(moved): Since Tuesday. Since they started saying it was the bird and
  I knew it was not the bird and I said nothing because she asked me not to.
  trust edwina 1
  goto edwina_asked

@node edwina_asked
  EDWINA(sad): I asked. She said, a thing that has a crack in it. She said it
  the way you say a thing you have decided not to cry about.
  set ch3.edwina_done = 1
  trust edwina 1

@node edwina_after
  [if flag ch3.edwina_done == 1]
  EDWINA: Bartleby has the histories. He will be unbearable about it and he
  will also be right.
  [else]
  EDWINA: The clock, first.
  goto edwina_ask
  [end]

@node bartleby_intro
  [if flag ch3.met_bartleby == 0]
  BARTLEBY(happy): A detective! In the reading room! I shall be insufferable
  about this for a year.
  YOU:
    * (kind) Be insufferable. I am in no hurry.  -> bartleby_indulge
    * (curious) I need the history of the Prism.  -> bartleby_history
    * (dry) You have about ten minutes of insufferable in you. Use it well.  -> bartleby_indulge
  [else]
  goto bartleby_after
  [end]

@node bartleby_indulge
  BARTLEBY(laughing): Oh, I like you. Nobody lets me finish.
  trust bartleby 1
  goto bartleby_history

@node bartleby_history
  set ch3.met_bartleby = 1
  BARTLEBY: The Prism does not make the colour. Everyone in this town will
  tell you it makes the colour. Everyone in this town is repeating their
  grandmother.
  BARTLEBY(worried): The Prism holds light. It is a jar, not a lamp. And a
  jar that is never filled is a jar that goes empty, slowly, over years, in a
  way nobody notices until a Tuesday.
  grant clue.prism_dimming
  YOU:
    * (curious) Filled by what?  -> bartleby_filled
    * (kind) Somebody noticed. Somebody always notices first.  -> bartleby_noticed
    * (dry) A jar. You have been waiting years to say that.  -> bartleby_filled

@node bartleby_noticed
  BARTLEBY(moved): ...Yes. And she sat in that chair, and she read what I have
  just told you, and she did not say one word about it to me.
  trust bartleby 1
  goto bartleby_filled

@node bartleby_filled
  BARTLEBY: By the Festival of Lanterns. The whole town on the green with a
  light each. That is the filling. That is the entire mechanism.
  BARTLEBY(worried): Which brings me to the shelf, and to my catalogue, and to
  a small joke played on me by my predecessor.
  BARTLEBY: The festival ledgers are shelved by a shifted alphabet. Turn the
  dial until the spine says something and I will hand you the gap.
  start_puzzle cipher_shelf
  BARTLEBY(happy): There. Reading is mostly turning things until they mean
  something.
  BARTLEBY(sad): And here is the gap. Forty years of ledgers in a row and then
  nothing. Three winters of nothing.
  grant clue.festival_lapsed
  set ch3.bartleby_done = 1
  trust bartleby 1

@node bartleby_after
  [if flag ch3.bartleby_done == 1]
  BARTLEBY: Petra Ward. Two doors down. She will tell you nothing at
  considerable length and you should listen to every word of the nothing.
  [else]
  BARTLEBY: The shelf, first.
  goto bartleby_filled
  [end]

@node petra_intro
  [if flag ch3.met_petra == 0]
  PETRA(neutral): Detective.
  PETRA: I know what you want and the answer is that I am not going to tell
  you.
  YOU:
    * (kind) Then I will not ask. Is that all right?  -> petra_notask
    * (curious) Your picks are missing and you reported nothing.  -> petra_picks
    * (dry) You have rehearsed that.  -> petra_rehearsed
  [else]
  goto petra_after
  [end]

@node petra_rehearsed
  PETRA(laughing): Twice. In the mirror. It came out better then.
  goto petra_picks

@node petra_notask
  PETRA(moved): ...That is not fair. That is much harder than being asked.
  trust petra 1
  goto petra_picks

@node petra_picks
  set ch3.met_petra = 1
  PETRA: My picks are not missing. There is a difference between a thing that
  is missing and a thing that is lent.
  grant clue.picks_borrowed
  YOU:
    * (curious) Lent to whom?  -> petra_whom
    * (kind) And you let the town call her a thief instead.  -> petra_town
    * (dry) You have let this whole street think you were robbed.  -> petra_town

@node petra_town
  PETRA(sad): The town is calling a bird a thief. Nobody has said her name
  once. I have listened for it.
  goto petra_whom

@node petra_whom
  PETRA(shifty): I gave my word. I gave it out loud, at that counter, and she
  did not even ask me to.
  grant clue.iris_secret
  PETRA: You may work it out. Working it out is not me telling you. I have
  thought about this a great deal in two days.
  PETRA(happy): And if you want to be able to work anything out, you should
  understand a lock properly. Sit down. This one is for teaching.
  start_puzzle tumbler_logic
  PETRA(moved): Good. Now you know that a lock is not a secret. It is a
  sentence you have not read yet.
  PETRA: She came in on the Thursday. She would not sit down. She asked to
  borrow the picks and she asked me not to tell anyone, and she was not
  frightened, she was embarrassed.
  YOU:
    * (curious) Embarrassed about what?  -> petra_embar
    * (kind) You have kept a hard promise for two days.  -> petra_hard
    * (dry) Embarrassed. Not the usual burglar's mood.  -> petra_embar

@node petra_hard
  PETRA(moved): I would keep it for twenty years. That is what a promise is.
  PETRA(sad): I would just rather somebody found her first.
  trust petra 1
  goto petra_done

@node petra_embar
  PETRA: I did not ask. She was holding the door frame with one hand and
  looking at the floor and I have known her since she was six.
  goto petra_done

@node petra_done
  set ch3.petra_done = 1
  trust petra 1

@node petra_after
  [if flag ch3.petra_done == 1]
  PETRA: You want to know why nobody has gathered on that green in three
  years. So do I. Ask the Gardens. Sage Fern says more than he means to.
  [else]
  PETRA: The teaching lock, first.
  goto petra_whom
  [end]
